  "articleBody": "Choosing between interlocking garage tiles and a bonded coating comes down to your slab condition, usage, and project turnaround. \n\nGarage Floor Coatings\nCoatings form a seamless barrier directly over concrete, making them simple to sweep clean. They resist oils and auto fluids well, but they demand rigorous surface preparation. The concrete must be degreased, repaired, and mechanically profiled between 40°F and 90°F. Curing can take 24 to 36 hours for vehicle traffic, or up to 120 hours in cold weather. New concrete must cure for about 30 days beforehand.\n\nGarage Floor Tiles\nInterlocking modular tiles install quickly over uneven slabs without chemical etching or long curing times. They handle heavy vehicle weights and accommodate minor surface cracks without transferring the flaw upward. However, tiles require perimeter movement gaps and conditioning at 72°F for 24 hours before installation so they do not buckle during seasonal temperature shifts.\n\nHow to Compare Your Options\nIf your slab is structurally sound and you want a continuous finish, a professionally applied coating is ideal. If your concrete has surface blemishes, or you need rapid vehicle turnaround without wet chemistry, tiles offer great flexibility. \n\nHH Remodeling LLC provides experienced garage remodel and floor installations across Denver and Aurora. Call 303-505-0866 to discuss your options with Abraham Becerra.",
